Calculate the time to collision (TTC) based on relative distance and speed. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
This function calculates the time to collision using the Uniformly Variable Motion (UVM) model. It uses a quadratic equation to calculate the time to collision (TTC) between two objects based on their relative distance and speed. If the relative acceleration is zero, the function simply calculates the time by dividing the relative distance by the relative speed [SwR-1] ({\b SwR-1}), [SwR-10], [SwR-11].\par
